meta {
  name: Connector Credentials - OAuth Callback
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/oauth/connectors/callback?state={{oauthState}}&code=auth-code-123
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  state: {{oauthState}}
  code: auth-code-123
}

docs {
  The provider's redirect target after the user approves OAuth access.
  Public (no session/API-key auth) — tenant-safety comes entirely from the
  unguessable `state` query param that `- OAuth Initiate` created, which
  is why this route lives outside `/v1` at the webhooks-style root
  `/oauth/connectors/callback` instead of under `/workspaces/{workspace}`.

  `code` is the provider's one-time authorization code; in practice this
  URL is hit by the browser redirect, not called manually. Deletes the
  `state` row on success and stores the resulting credential.

  Response is wrapped (201):
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { connector_credential } }`.
}
